.Dd June 6, 2026
.Dt LOCALPORTS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm localports
.Nd inspect local TCP ports and safely free them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar port
.Nm
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -verbose
.Op Fl -tree
.Op Fl -docker
.Nm
.Fl w
.Op Ar seconds
.Nm
.Fl k Ar port
.Op Fl -all | Fl -pid Ar pid
.Op Fl f
.Nm
.Fl -kill-pid Ar pid
.Op Fl f
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists listening TCP ports on macOS using libproc directly.
It is designed for a developer's daily workflow: quickly answer what owns a
port, why it exists, and what can be safely done about it.
.Pp
By default, output is a human-readable table.
The JSON shape is stable unless extra fields are requested with display flags.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p , Fl -port Ar port
Filter by port number.
A bare positional
.Ar port
is also accepted.
.It Fl -json
Output machine-readable JSON.
.It Fl -verbose
Show the owning user and full command line.
Some process details require ownership or root privileges.
.It Fl -tree
Show each listener's parent-process chain, immediate parent first.
.It Fl -docker
Resolve Docker-owned host ports to the publishing container.
.It Fl w , Fl -watch Op Ar seconds
Refresh continuously.
The default interval is 2 seconds; values below 1 are clamped to 1.
Watch mode is table-only.
.It Fl k , Fl -kill Ar port
Kill the process listening on
.Ar port .
If more than one process matches, refuse to choose automatically.
If the selected listener is a Docker host process, refuse so Docker Desktop is
not killed in place of the publishing container.
.It Fl a , Fl -all
With
.Fl -kill Ar port ,
kill every matching process.
.It Fl -pid Ar pid
With
.Fl -kill Ar port ,
kill only
.Ar pid
if it is listening on the selected port.
.It Fl -kill-pid Ar pid
Kill a process by explicit PID without a port lookup.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Skip kill confirmation.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Show version.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show help.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Error, including invalid arguments, no matching listener, permission denied,
ambiguous kill refusal, or a failed kill.
.It 2
Kill confirmation declined.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li localports
List all listening TCP ports.
.It Li localports 3000
Show listeners on port 3000.
.It Li localports --verbose --tree
Show owners, command lines, and parent-process chains.
.It Li localports 5432 --docker
Resolve a Docker-published port to its container.
.It Li localports --kill 3000
Safely terminate the sole listener on port 3000.
.It Li localports --kill 8000 --pid 6524
Kill a specific PID only if it is listening on port 8000.
.El
.Sh JSON CONTRACT
Default JSON rows contain:
.Pp
.Dl {"port":8000,"pid":6524,"proto":"tcp","process":"Python","address":"127.0.0.1"}
.Pp
.Fl -verbose
adds
.Sy user
and
.Sy command .
.Fl -tree
adds
.Sy ancestors .
.Fl -docker
adds
.Sy container .
These fields are emitted only when their flags are present.
.Sh NOTES
.Nm
supports macOS today.
Run with
.Sy sudo
to see process details owned by other users.
